WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.890
Two postcards slide onto a desk.

2
00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:07.580
One in Victorian copperplate,
one glowing on a phone screen.

3
00:00:07.630 --> 00:00:12.790
A question card drops between them:
"What do both writers find at the lake?"

4
00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:14.840
So you start copying.

5
00:00:14.890 --> 00:00:16.680
Line after line.

6
00:00:16.730 --> 00:00:20.820
The answer box overflows,
and the clock keeps ticking.

7
00:00:20.870 --> 00:00:25.300
How do you sum up two texts in
a few lines, without copying?

8
00:00:25.350 --> 00:00:29.480
In this mission, you'll find out what
summary and synthesis really mean,

9
00:00:29.530 --> 00:00:31.080
and how they differ.

10
00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:32.870
Retell each text in order?

11
00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:35.400
Copy the key sentences as evidence?

12
00:00:35.450 --> 00:00:37.680
You'll test both against the question.

13
00:00:37.730 --> 00:00:40.790
And you'll weigh up answers
about two lake visits,

14
00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:44.350
one written in 1873 and one today.

15
00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:48.280
Your mission: work out how to
sum them up without copying.
